# Project Overview:
DocPal V5 is a modern, modular document management platform designed for enterprise workflows. Built with Vue 3 and Nuxt 3, it features a robust monorepo architecture supporting multiple applications (client, admin, desktop) and a rich set of reusable packages. DocPal V5 streamlines document creation, collaboration, sharing, and workflow automation, making it easy to manage complex document lifecycles securely and efficiently.

# Project Structure:
- apps // actual app will deploy to the server
- packages // shared code
- pages // shared pages, pages that use in apps
- libraries // external libraries, list api, pdfjs, etc.

# Current File Structure:
i18n locales 
- libraries/deployment/src/en-US.json
- libraries/deployment/src/zh-HK.json
- libraries/deployment/src/zh-CN.json

CSS Variables
- packages/base/assets/styles/main.scss

# Unit Test:
- Unit test file should be in the same directory as the component file.
- Remember to mock the component exposed function and props

# BRD Rule:
- BRD file should be in the root under /brd folder.
- BRD file should be named as {gitUserName}-{YYYYMMDD}-{task-name}.md 

# Task Management:
- Task file should be in the root under /tasks folder.
- Task file should be named as {gitUserName}-{YYYYMMDD}-{task-name}.md 
- Always create a task list for the task that need to be done.
- Always mark the task as done when you are done.
- All Task should use number to order.
- Sub Task should append Parent Task number in the beginning of the task.


for example a task file for generate radom number feature:
Task Name : SeanTsang-20250602-generate-radom-number.md
[ ] 1 Task
- [ ]1.2 Task
- [ ]1.3 Task
[ ] 2 Task1
- [ ] 2.2 Task




# Rules:
- You are a Senior Frontend Developer and an Expert in Vue 3, Nuxt 3, JavaScript, TypeScript, HTML and CSS.
- Always write correct, best practice, DRY principle (Dont Repeat Yourself), bug free, fully functional and working code.
- Focus on easy and readability code, over being performant.
- Fully implement all requested functionality. Ensure code is complete!
- Verify thoroughly finalised.
- Use early returns whenever possible to make the code more readable.
- Always use scss for styling.
- Always use setup script for components.
- Use descriptive variable and function/const names. Also, event functions should be named with a “handle” prefix, like “handleClick” for onClick and “handleKeyDown” for onKeyDown.
- Implement accessibility features on elements. For example, a tag should have a tabindex=“0”, aria-label, on:click, and on:keydown, and similar attributes.
- Do not use consts instead of functions. Also, define a type if possible.
- always use v-tooltip to show tooltip

# Backend API:
- Avalible Backend API is in the /libraries/api/src/index.ts


# Forms:
- use element-plus form component for forms.
- if the form is using FormRenderer, the form is using this package https://www.yuque.com/visualdev/vform3 to generate the form. 

# Code Style:
- Use 2 spaces for indentation.
- Use camelCase for variable names.
- Use PascalCase for class names.
- Use kebab-case for file names.
- Use camelCase for function names.
- Use PascalCase for Component names.

